# A8.3 — DOES A PART READ AS A DOOR, WITH NOTHING BUT CELLS IN IT?
#
# `door.keys` asks the same question of the editor's own wall-opening gesture. This
# asks it of a PART: a doorway authored in `data/parts/`, opened in part mode, and
# photographed from where a person would stand.
#
# ⚠ PART MODE IS THE ONLY PLACE THIS PICTURE EXISTS. `14:<roof>,<part>` in a WORLD
# stamps the named part's own cells and expands nothing — no instance, no limb — so
# a doorway placed that way is its paving and nothing else. `44:` swaps the store
# and the display world IS the expansion, which is what puts the frame and the leaf
# in one picture.
#
# ⚠ AND THE CAMERA HAS TO BE PLACED AFTER THE SWAP. The part is three hexes across
# at the origin; the author standing where a world put them is outside it looking at
# nothing.

echo --- flat ground, so the swap has something to come back to
at 0 0 0
key ArrowUp
wait rebuilt

echo --- open the doorway as a part
send 44:door/planked
wait part

# ⚠ THE PAIR BELOW IS AN INSTRUMENT CHECK, NOT TWO VIEWS. A limb's mesh id is
# 5..15 and the client's `mesh_bit` answers `1` — the FIGURE's bit — for every id at
# or below 15. So EYES, which is the obvious way to get the walker out of the
# picture, hides the leaf along with the body: the first shot taken that way was a
# paving slab with nothing standing on it, and it read as *the limb is not drawn*
# while the wire said it had been. AUTO is the mode that can see this subject.
echo --- AUTO, from far enough back that the walker is not the subject
# ⚠ THE MODE IS SET, NEVER ASSUMED. A server keeps its state between runs, so the
# first version of this script photographed a station it had left in EYES on the
# previous run and labelled the picture AUTO. The subject line in the shot is the
# control: it names the mode the server thinks it is in.
send 40:0
wait mode
at 2.598 -6.0 90
snap a83-doorway

echo --- the same station in EYES, which by construction cannot see a limb
send 40:4
wait mode
snap a83-doorway-eyes
send 40:0
wait mode

echo --- from the side, where a swung leaf casts its line
at -2.5 1.5 0
snap a83-doorway-side

echo --- back to the world, so nothing is left open
send 44:
wait part
